@startuml cue-playback
' SPEC: _spec/apps/starchess/timeline/cue-playback.puml
' purpose: playTimeline dispatch — how the head of the cue queue picks a
' handler, what each handler commits, and when the board ladder advances.
' covers: apps/starchess/src/__tests__/timelinePlayer.test.ts
!include ../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · ""playTimeline"" — dispatch and commit semantics

start
:commit the ""afterPending"" board + pre-shot king HP;
note right
  ""livesBeforeAnimatedShots"" **undoes** the chips ""afterPending"" already
  applied, so a king hull stays pristine until frag impact. Only turn-open
  chips are undone — classical chips live in ""next"" and land at impact
  without an undo.
end note
if (no cues?) then (yes)
  :apply ""afterB"", commit ""next"", done;
  stop
endif

repeat :read cue at ""index"", ""takeWhile"" its batch;

  if (gas drop?) then (yes)
    :absorb window — pull an adjacent deploy batch and its crush deaths\ninto the **same** window so a trailing attack cannot clip the drop;
    :crush deaths start ~""CRUSH_DEATH_MS"" into the deploy (mid-drop\ncollapse), window = max(gas, deploy, crush);
    :stamp ""U:"" aura squares on completion;
  elseif (spawn deploy?) then (yes)
    :same shape without the canister (auto-deploy / edge cases);
    :**late windows** (F wave, after moves/attacks mutated placement)\npatch the board **forward** (""commitDeployBoard"") — re-applying\n""afterB"" would rewind relocates and resurrect the dead;
  elseif (phase-1 attack?) then (yes)
    :one window for **both** sides' shots; deaths overlap at the max\nper-weapon ""attackImpactMs"" so impact meets collapse;
    :ccShot HP lands at that impact (the damage boom syncs to the hit);
    :reciprocal fire → ""attackDying"" suppresses the attacker hull so the\ndeath animation owns the square; flags held until the wave ends so\nhulls cannot flash back;
    :mine cleared by an attack → ""spentMines"" hides the glyph as the boom\nstarts (the mine stays in the snapshot until ""afterAttack"");
    :deaths done → stamp ""afterAttack"" but keep the attack cues mounted\nuntil ""ATTACK_MS"" (clearing early truncates the shot);
  elseif (phase-1 death, no attack ahead of it?) then (yes)
    :fallback window, then stamp ""afterAttack"";
  elseif (chase missile?) then (yes)
    :trails + ""spentMines"" for the wake tile; the mine snapshot comes from\n""cue.board"" — ""afterMove"" for a phase-3 chase, ""afterAttack"" otherwise;
    :trails outlive the cue (CSS fade cleared later, fire-and-forget);
  elseif (move-collision death?) then (yes)
    :only when no wave absorbed it (see the move wave below): death window,\nthen vacate the square in ""displayPlacement"";
    :a mine among them takes ""spentMines"" too — this lane's ""mineBlast""\nbranch has no producer today, kept honest rather than exercised;
  elseif (mine-trigger death — phase 2 **and** phase-3 approach?) then (yes)
    :commit the ""afterMove"" mine snapshot + ""spentMines"" for the boom tile\n(plus the wake tile a chase left behind), then vacate;
  elseif (simultaneous move wave?) then (yes)
    :group by ""cue.group"" — B gas steps, classical, F steps each form one\nwave; opposing sides move together;
    :progress 0 → 1 on the next frame drives the slide; knights flip their\nleg at the elbow; a hoverbike/battleship wave is held one SETTLE_MS\npast touchdown so the aim→rest unwind lands before hand-off;\nwindow = slowest cue in the batch + that settle hold;
    :**collisions meet at contact** — the wave absorbs the collision deaths\nthat follow it when every one sits on a square ≥ 2 of its movers target\n(core already ends both movers' ""to"" on ""moverContact"".at). A square's\ncontact is the later mover's arrival (""cueDuration"", no settle): there the\ndying movers leave ""playingIds"", vanish from ""displayPlacement"" (the\nboard derives hides from playing cues, so a kept origin would reappear),\nand the square's deaths play for DEATH_MS. A survivor (a Command Center\nthat took the unit) keeps sliding and relocates at the end. Window =\nmax(survivors + settle, contact + DEATH_MS); a wave with no collision\nkeeps the old window.;
  elseif (promo walk-off / promo deploy?) then (yes)
    :walk-offs in parallel (square vacated at the end), then deploys —\npromoted units are placed **before** the deploy animation so nothing\ndownstream sees a late spawn after ""TIMELINE_DONE"";
  else (sequential tail)
    :approach chains, Tactical Jump, arrival blasts and any leftover cue\nplay one at a time;
    :a mine death here — ""armm"" / ""qjm"" / ""farmm"", the rungs with no\nbatching handler of their own — takes ""spentMines"" for its tile;
    :a lethal ccShot immediately followed by its king death is fused —\nthe king crumples at frag impact instead of after the full shot;
    :Tactical Jump owns its own travel + trail timing (never a slide);
    :any death vacates its square on completion so a corpse cannot flash\nback between the death VFX and an occupy that follows;
  endif

  :advance the board ladder **lazily**: a cue whose ""cue.board"" is past\n""preAfterB"" applies ""afterB""; nothing re-applies a rung;
  note right
    ""afterB"" is committed as ""afterBDisplay"" — the same board with every
    ""resolved.promotions"" square **rewound to a marine**.

    A gas promotion resolves inside ""submit-turn"" (""applyGasPromotion"" and
    the F-step path), which writes the promoted unit straight into ""afterB"".
    Showing that rung verbatim deploys the unit, then the promo walk-off
    yanks it away, then the promo deploy plays it again — one promotion,
    two deploys.

    Core stays right: everything after B must treat the square as a queen.
    Only the **display** board rewinds, and only per-square where ""afterB""
    actually holds that promotion's unit — a blanket rewrite would plant a
    phantom pawn on a *classical* promotion's destination, where the pawn
    has not moved yet at B.

    With no promotions it returns ""afterB.placement"" itself, preserving the
    object identity ""commitDeployBoard"" branches on.
  end note

  note right
    **Every lane that plays a ""mine: true"" death owes ""spentMines""**
    (""spentMineSquares""). ""hidden"" gates piece glyphs only; the mine glyph is
    gated by ""StarChessBoard.showMine()"", which reads ""spentMines"" — so a lane
    that forgets it leaves an intact mine drawn **under** its own wreck.
    Omitting the field on a commit means *keep* (""withSquareList""), so one
    commit at boom start covers the window; the list resets with the resolve.
  end note

repeat while (more cues?) is (yes)
->no;
:finalize → commit ""next"" (placement, HP, mines, siege, ""U:"") and ""onDone"".\nWith ""finalize: false"" (mid-wave tutorial) stop at the last rung reached;
note right
  **Cancellation contract:** every scheduled callback is registered in
  ""cancels"" and every callback re-checks the ""cancelled"" flag before it
  commits. The returned disposer flips the flag and drains the list. A handler
  that schedules work without registering it leaks a commit past teardown —
   the one rule that must survive any refactor of this file.

   **The scheduler is injected** (""Scheduler"" port), so tests drive the whole
   timeline deterministically with a fake clock — no real timers, no flake.
 end note

' N_ATTACK_DYING: reciprocal fire suppresses attacker hull on at==from
note right
  Reciprocal fire suppresses the attacker
  hull exactly when death.at matches the
  attack.from square. Flags persist until
  the attack wave clears, never flicker.
end note

' N_JUMP_TRAIL: Jump trails linger 1000ms past hull clear
note right
  Tactical Jump trails persist 1000ms past
  hull collapse for the CSS fade. onDone
  fires at hull clear, never waits fade.
end note
stop
@enduml
